      "scope": "Real child processes/default liveness and filesystem expose two simultaneous unreleased live grants. Real non-root permissions separately expose a silent failed release and a wrongly quarantined genuinely live legacy owner. Original failures remain retained."
    },
    "do": [
      "Reuse already bundled SQLite as one stable per-action OS-backed guard. Keep its connection/callback in the existing manager until authorized release settles. Different actions remain independent; no schema, WAL, helper, dependency or background scheduler is introduced. SQLite owns its transient rollback journal.",
      "Place main/sidecar below the existing denied .keiko segment, including custom state roots. Ordinary raw/resolved workspace readers refuse it; existing scan/snapshot/repair inspect metadata/counts/modes only. No raw guard body reads, hashing, unlink, quarantine or recreation. Existing pathname-only SQLite preflight limits remain explicit.",
      "Reuse the existing bounded state-file descriptor reader for canonical records:4KiB cap, nonblocking/no-follow regular single-link admission, exact BigInt held/name/change checks, and content-specific UTF8/JSON parsing. Actual malformed content retains existing publication grace; IO/unsafe/changed ownership refuses without quarantine.",
      "Propagate failed release read/rename/unlink. Retain the exact requested callback/guard for a later explicit same-manager retry before new admission. Never retry an unrequested uncertain-outcome hold; old callbacks cannot retire replacement entries.",
      "Extend the existing update-runtime Activity Log class with closed lease states, opaque attempt ID, action digest and originating correlation; reuse existing ports/diagnostics and strengthen its canonical lifecycle/causal/proof/resource obligations. Canonical generators produce registries; two obsolete catch-register entries are deleted."
    ],
